Aim

To create and launch a YouTube Ads campaign using Google Ads.

Beginner Level Exact Steps
Step 1: Open Browser

Open Google Chrome.

Step 2: Open Google Ads Website

Go to:

Google Ads

Step 3: Login with Gmail
Enter Gmail ID
Enter password
Login successfully
Step 4: Open YouTube

Open:

YouTube

Step 5: Upload a Video to YouTube
Click Create
Click Upload Video
Select any sample video
Enter:
Title
Description
Click Publish

Example:

Food Delivery Advertisement
Step 6: Create New Campaign in Google Ads
Return to Google Ads
Click New Campaign
Step 7: Select Campaign Goal

Choose any goal:

Website traffic
Sales
Brand awareness

Example:

Brand Awareness
Step 8: Select Video Campaign

Choose:

Video Campaign

This is used for YouTube advertisements.

Step 9: Set Campaign Details

Enter:

Campaign name
Budget
Start date
End date

Example:

Field	Example
Campaign Name	Food Delivery Ads
Budget	₹100 per day
Step 10: Select Target Audience

Choose:

Age group
Gender
Location
Interests

Example:

18–35 years
Step 11: Add YouTube Video Link
Copy uploaded YouTube video URL
Paste in Google Ads video section

Example:

https://youtube.com/examplevideo
Step 12: Create Advertisement

Enter:

Final URL
Headline
Call To Action
Example
Field	Example
Headline	Order Food Online
CTA	Order Now
Step 13: Preview Advertisement

Google Ads shows preview:

Mobile view
Desktop view

Check advertisement appearance.

Step 14: Publish Campaign

Click:

Publish Campaign

Campaign created successfully.

Step 15: Take Screenshots

Take screenshots of:

Campaign page
Video upload
Audience settings
Ad preview

(Useful for practical record)
